WEBVTT

00:00:02.830 --> 00:00:08.090
(Chūka Ichiban)

00:01:33.630 --> 00:01:35.190
When Lei En and I

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:37.380
were battling for the legendary cookware,

00:01:38.270 --> 00:01:39.630
his dishes

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:41.100
cooked with seven knives

00:01:41.640 --> 00:01:43.580
tied with

00:01:45.130 --> 00:01:46.720
my Chinese mainland in Pagrus Major.

00:01:47.110 --> 00:01:48.960
Then he demanded a fence-off

00:01:49.390 --> 00:01:50.860
and drew out the secret knife of the Dark Cooking Society,

00:01:51.180 --> 00:01:53.480
the North Star Sirius Blade.

00:01:54.840 --> 00:01:57.160
The previous rounds are only warm-ups.

00:01:57.450 --> 00:01:58.700
My following dish

00:01:59.260 --> 00:02:01.660
will give you a taste of heaven!

00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:10.950
Ice and Fire Ultimate Battle of Spirits

00:02:14.070 --> 00:02:15.330
North Star Sirius Blade!

00:02:17.720 --> 00:02:19.030
Arhat Crystal Slice!

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:24.310
(Arhat Crystal Slice)

00:02:41.900 --> 00:02:43.990
That knife is incredibly sharp!

00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:46.480
Its speed and precision

00:02:46.680 --> 00:02:48.200
have surpassed that of the previous ones!

00:02:48.250 --> 00:02:49.870
On top of that,

00:02:50.580 --> 00:02:52.840
the look on his face is most intimidating!

00:02:57.870 --> 00:02:59.830
I can feel his strength from afar.

00:02:59.880 --> 00:03:00.700
Well...

00:03:00.770 --> 00:03:01.600
As far as I’m concerned,

00:03:01.650 --> 00:03:03.520
he’s just making

00:03:03.560 --> 00:03:05.550
another sashimi.

00:03:06.510 --> 00:03:07.210
What do you know,

00:03:07.360 --> 00:03:08.660
you four old geezers?

00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:09.670
Excuse me?

00:03:10.130 --> 00:03:11.490
Take a good look at yourselves

00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:13.790
with my thin slices.

00:03:28.130 --> 00:03:28.900
No way!

00:03:29.250 --> 00:03:30.490
That’s us!

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:34.750
Those slices reflect our faces!

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:38.740
As rough as Mao was

00:03:38.790 --> 00:03:39.800
with that fish,

00:03:40.340 --> 00:03:41.540
it wasn’t damaged a bit.

00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:45.630
Each slice is as transparent as a mirror.

00:03:46.170 --> 00:03:48.740
I can’t believe that kind of skill is real!

00:03:51.830 --> 00:03:53.100
The glare of that knife,

00:03:54.150 --> 00:03:55.440
the exquisitely clean cut

00:03:56.050 --> 00:03:58.470
and Lei En’s grimace...

00:03:59.170 --> 00:04:00.570
It... it can’t be...

00:04:01.700 --> 00:04:02.910
No, that must be it!

00:04:03.560 --> 00:04:04.770
What’s up, Chef Xie?

00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:06.210
That knife with dark secrets...

00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:07.580
the North Star Sirius Blade...

00:04:07.860 --> 00:04:08.920
What about it?

00:04:09.260 --> 00:04:10.730
It’s made of ice.

00:04:14.230 --> 00:04:15.430
A cooking knife made of ice?

00:04:15.530 --> 00:04:16.420
Impossible!

00:04:16.570 --> 00:04:17.710
Guangzhou is too warm

00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:19.350
for ice to freeze.

00:04:19.620 --> 00:04:21.620
If it was ice, the whole thing would’ve melted.

00:04:22.370 --> 00:04:24.040
It’s true. I’ve heard about it.

00:04:25.210 --> 00:04:28.040
It’s said that the Dark Cooking Society

00:04:28.480 --> 00:04:29.570
spent years

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:30.380
making a knife

00:04:30.430 --> 00:04:31.580
in the cold

00:04:31.630 --> 00:04:36.570
with ice from a glacier in the north.

00:04:38.650 --> 00:04:40.340
It’s made of ice?

00:04:41.220 --> 00:04:42.650
I've learned about it, too.

00:04:43.690 --> 00:04:44.400
That knife

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:46.310
is tailor-made to be as sharp as a razor.

00:04:47.060 --> 00:04:48.330
Meanwhile, the icy blade

00:04:48.670 --> 00:04:51.180
can keep the meat fresh.

00:04:51.230 --> 00:04:52.790
So it’s a perfect knife for cooking.

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:54.760
If so,

00:04:54.800 --> 00:04:56.560
why didn’t Lei En

00:04:56.610 --> 00:04:58.360
use it in the beginning?

00:04:58.740 --> 00:05:01.380
Check out his hand.

00:05:07.250 --> 00:05:09.860
His right hand looks bruised.

00:05:09.960 --> 00:05:10.500
Is that...?

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:12.220
Yes, that’s frostbite.

00:05:13.460 --> 00:05:15.810
The low temperate

00:05:15.880 --> 00:05:17.750
is damaging his tissue.

00:05:21.560 --> 00:05:23.700
Is it worth it?

00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:25.010
He could’ve wrapped his hand

00:05:25.060 --> 00:05:26.620
with a piece of cloth or something.

00:05:27.370 --> 00:05:28.760
As skilled as he is,

00:05:28.980 --> 00:05:31.730
the cloth might affect his sense of touch.

00:05:32.630 --> 00:05:34.340
He could only

00:05:34.510 --> 00:05:35.300
hold that knife barehanded

00:05:35.350 --> 00:05:36.770
to reach that level of perfection.

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:38.570
Must he do that?

00:05:39.310 --> 00:05:40.500
A chef like him is risking his right hand

00:05:40.550 --> 00:05:43.090
to win.

00:05:43.870 --> 00:05:45.190
The North Star Sirius Blade

00:05:45.800 --> 00:05:47.290
is a double-edged sword.

00:05:48.650 --> 00:05:50.490
Is that the Dark Cooking Society’s style?

00:05:50.830 --> 00:05:52.500
Like the Japanese samurai warrior

00:05:52.550 --> 00:05:54.240
my mother once told me about.

00:05:54.820 --> 00:05:57.790
Such a huge price for some cookware?

00:05:57.790 --> 00:06:00.000
Lei En is too obsessed!

00:06:03.550 --> 00:06:04.200
Mao...

00:06:04.370 --> 00:06:05.820
What’s his plan?

00:06:11.890 --> 00:06:12.660
Do something!

00:06:12.700 --> 00:06:13.620
What’s he going to do

00:06:13.670 --> 00:06:15.750
with the same knives?

00:06:52.140 --> 00:06:53.480
His fish exploded!

00:06:54.010 --> 00:06:54.600
One cut

00:06:54.650 --> 00:06:56.740
and boom!

00:06:57.340 --> 00:06:59.300
What did he do?

00:07:02.590 --> 00:07:03.470
He’s doing it again!

00:07:09.100 --> 00:07:12.160
Did he put gunpowder in it?

00:07:12.560 --> 00:07:13.190
If he did,

00:07:13.240 --> 00:07:14.570
the flesh would’ve been ruined!

00:07:14.710 --> 00:07:16.410
It must be something on the knife that did it.

00:07:16.910 --> 00:07:19.260
No way. I made a knife,

00:07:19.380 --> 00:07:20.690
not a bomb.

00:07:21.060 --> 00:07:23.540
So what exactly did he do?

00:07:31.850 --> 00:07:32.590
Finished!

00:07:41.490 --> 00:07:43.790
Mao’s knife is sparkling.

00:07:44.450 --> 00:07:46.500
What... what is that?

00:07:55.840 --> 00:07:57.020
Steel wire!

00:07:57.450 --> 00:07:59.650
He made a little handle

00:08:00.010 --> 00:08:02.720
over each hole with the steel wires.

00:08:05.260 --> 00:08:06.040
I got it!

00:08:06.090 --> 00:08:06.830
That explains

00:08:07.290 --> 00:08:09.340
the explosion!

00:08:10.250 --> 00:08:11.700
Sharp handles on the surface

00:08:11.750 --> 00:08:13.460
squeezed the meat out

00:08:13.710 --> 00:08:15.860
instantly.

00:08:16.640 --> 00:08:17.570
And the swing shot the mince

00:08:17.620 --> 00:08:19.850
into the air

00:08:20.290 --> 00:08:22.060
as if the meat exploded.

00:08:22.840 --> 00:08:24.400
I see.

00:08:25.020 --> 00:08:26.430
You're a genius, Mao!

00:08:27.040 --> 00:08:28.940
How clever he is

00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:31.200
by using those two knives to make a new one!

00:08:31.250 --> 00:08:33.680
I agree! I’m in awe of him!

00:08:34.190 --> 00:08:34.690
That new tool

00:08:34.740 --> 00:08:36.060
tenderized the meat

00:08:36.160 --> 00:08:38.150
in the blink of an eye.

00:08:38.700 --> 00:08:39.550
Good job, Mao!

00:08:40.220 --> 00:08:41.150
Your new knife

00:08:41.200 --> 00:08:42.780
is as efficient as Lei En’s ice knife!

00:08:42.860 --> 00:08:44.400
It worked like magic!

00:08:44.600 --> 00:08:46.270
Yes!

00:08:47.860 --> 00:08:48.400
Kid,

00:08:48.740 --> 00:08:50.860
don’t you know how big a mistake you made?

00:08:51.830 --> 00:08:53.900
Never mince such fine fish,

00:08:54.300 --> 00:08:55.430
or it’ll taste bad.

00:08:56.050 --> 00:08:57.540
How are you going to fix that?

00:08:58.300 --> 00:08:59.270
I know what I’m doing.

00:08:59.700 --> 00:09:00.320
What?

00:09:01.190 --> 00:09:02.440
I’ll bring this fish

00:09:02.670 --> 00:09:04.170
back to life.

00:09:04.730 --> 00:09:06.070
Listen to yourself!

00:09:06.400 --> 00:09:07.680
A chef’s knife is supposed to

00:09:07.730 --> 00:09:08.870
bring out the taste

00:09:09.260 --> 00:09:10.230
of the ingredient itself

00:09:10.280 --> 00:09:11.390
to the maximum.

00:09:12.610 --> 00:09:13.530
That punk

00:09:13.580 --> 00:09:15.270
is finding fault with Mao!

00:09:16.000 --> 00:09:18.880
Ignore him, Mao!

00:09:18.930 --> 00:09:20.920
Yes! Ignore him!

00:09:21.350 --> 00:09:22.720
It’s wise to form a new tool

00:09:22.760 --> 00:09:25.370
against Lei En’s secret knife,

00:09:25.990 --> 00:09:26.910
but Mao,

00:09:27.370 --> 00:09:29.210
you've forgotten the most important thing.

00:09:30.460 --> 00:09:32.120
Mao is cutting vegetables

00:09:32.720 --> 00:09:33.620
into shreds.

00:09:34.010 --> 00:09:35.560
He’s going to mix them with the mince.

00:09:35.750 --> 00:09:38.240
But he's already heating the pot.

00:09:39.610 --> 00:09:40.240
Usually, the mince

00:09:40.290 --> 00:09:42.450
needs raw coriander and spices.

00:09:43.120 --> 00:09:43.850
What’s that?

00:09:44.660 --> 00:09:45.470
Bamboo shoots...

00:09:45.760 --> 00:09:46.750
Shiitake mushrooms...

00:09:47.170 --> 00:09:48.040
Carrots...

00:09:51.780 --> 00:09:53.400
What’s he going to do

00:09:53.450 --> 00:09:55.150
with those vegetable shreds?

00:10:22.760 --> 00:10:23.650
Oh, no!

00:10:30.170 --> 00:10:32.050
His hand is severely injured!

00:10:32.860 --> 00:10:34.870
That man is no quitter!

00:10:35.000 --> 00:10:36.160
Rest in peace.

00:10:45.790 --> 00:10:48.150
There you are, Lei En.

00:10:48.490 --> 00:10:50.210
You buried livestock again.

00:10:51.090 --> 00:10:52.250
They have lives

00:10:52.550 --> 00:10:53.990
just like humans.

00:10:54.890 --> 00:10:56.190
We live on

00:10:56.370 --> 00:10:57.690
by killing them.

00:10:58.560 --> 00:10:59.230
All I can do

00:10:59.640 --> 00:11:01.420
is to make sure they rest in peace.

00:11:03.940 --> 00:11:04.790
He’s still the same.

00:11:05.660 --> 00:11:08.230
Lei En hasn’t changed a bit.

00:11:14.840 --> 00:11:15.890
It's time.

00:11:38.050 --> 00:11:39.490
Please taste my dish

00:11:40.460 --> 00:11:43.180
while that kid is still working on his.

00:11:43.980 --> 00:11:45.090
Now is the best time

00:11:45.840 --> 00:11:47.460
to give you a taste of the freshness.

00:11:48.930 --> 00:11:50.770
Meet my ultra-fresh sashimi,

00:11:51.110 --> 00:11:52.630
the Ice Pagrus Major Mountain!

00:12:05.140 --> 00:12:07.010
(Chūka Ichiban)

00:12:13.420 --> 00:12:15.020
The Ice Pagrus Major Mountain!

00:12:15.020 --> 00:12:18.110
(Ice Pagrus Major Mountain)

00:12:20.490 --> 00:12:21.730
That’s a lot of ice.

00:12:22.790 --> 00:12:23.530
Where’s the fish?

00:12:23.780 --> 00:12:25.740
I don’t see any of it.

00:12:26.190 --> 00:12:27.550
Look again.

00:12:35.940 --> 00:12:37.210
The super thin slices

00:12:37.250 --> 00:12:39.060
are glued to the ice.

00:12:39.110 --> 00:12:41.690
The ice must’ve come from the ice knife.

00:12:42.060 --> 00:12:43.490
It’s mere decoration, isn’t it?

00:12:44.960 --> 00:12:46.620
No, it’s not.

00:12:47.240 --> 00:12:48.170
Sashimi

00:12:48.570 --> 00:12:49.700
should remain iced

00:12:49.750 --> 00:12:50.990
until it goes into the mouth.

00:12:51.040 --> 00:12:52.170
It tastes the best that way.

00:12:52.790 --> 00:12:55.480
Dip the slice into this sauce with sesame oil

00:12:55.960 --> 00:12:58.810
and you’ll be on cloud nine.

00:12:59.910 --> 00:13:02.190
You’re exaggerating it!

00:13:28.010 --> 00:13:29.260
The knife with dark secrets,

00:13:29.510 --> 00:13:30.810
the North Star Sirius Blade,

00:13:32.120 --> 00:13:33.100
will show you

00:13:34.530 --> 00:13:35.400
its real magic!

00:13:39.570 --> 00:13:40.440
There’s wind!

00:13:43.580 --> 00:13:44.710
Like the Arctic blizzard

00:13:44.830 --> 00:13:48.020
in my mouth!

00:13:53.710 --> 00:13:54.830
The wind will stop soon.

00:13:55.960 --> 00:13:57.790
The taste of life

00:13:58.100 --> 00:14:01.350
is breaking through the ice,

00:14:01.970 --> 00:14:03.060
following the coolness.

00:14:06.960 --> 00:14:08.850
When the warm cavity meets the cold meat,

00:14:08.980 --> 00:14:10.750
its smooth and refreshing taste

00:14:10.800 --> 00:14:12.910
fills the mouth immediately.

00:14:14.840 --> 00:14:17.100
That kind of tenderness is beyond words.

00:14:17.140 --> 00:14:18.640
It’s the supreme taste!

00:14:24.490 --> 00:14:26.820
It’s as if

00:14:27.380 --> 00:14:28.790
the frozen fish came back alive,

00:14:28.840 --> 00:14:30.360
bouncing in my mouth!

00:14:37.000 --> 00:14:38.820
It does taste like heaven!

00:14:39.080 --> 00:14:44.630
(Supreme Taste) (Heaven)
(Heavenly Enjoyment)

00:14:54.980 --> 00:14:58.790
The key

00:14:58.900 --> 00:15:00.270
to this masterpiece

00:15:00.390 --> 00:15:01.550
is the timing.

00:15:02.320 --> 00:15:04.030
It’s been six hours

00:15:04.140 --> 00:15:06.340
since this fish was caught at sunrise.

00:15:06.490 --> 00:15:09.110
And now is the golden time

00:15:09.160 --> 00:15:11.780
to savor it.

00:15:12.580 --> 00:15:13.870
You’ve captured the gist

00:15:14.060 --> 00:15:16.090
and delivered it perfectly.

00:15:17.240 --> 00:15:19.130
You did an excellent job, Lei En!

00:15:21.660 --> 00:15:23.490
Mao still has a shot, doesn’t he?

00:15:24.180 --> 00:15:24.900
How come he’s still

00:15:24.950 --> 00:15:27.640
looking at Lei En’s dish?

00:15:30.830 --> 00:15:31.910
Sorry for the wait.

00:15:35.940 --> 00:15:38.580
Your dish took a longer time.

00:15:38.920 --> 00:15:39.920
I apologize for the delay.

00:15:40.830 --> 00:15:41.530
Please enjoy.

00:15:50.850 --> 00:15:56.430
Those... those are spring rolls?

00:15:57.200 --> 00:15:59.450
Correct. Liu Maoxing presents:

00:15:59.900 --> 00:16:01.190
The Reincarnation Spring Rolls!

00:16:02.410 --> 00:16:03.920
(Reincarnation Spring Rolls)

00:16:04.390 --> 00:16:05.660
Wow!

00:16:06.090 --> 00:16:07.660
So he minced the whole part

00:16:07.710 --> 00:16:11.060
to make spring rolls.

00:16:11.170 --> 00:16:12.460
I see.

00:16:12.930 --> 00:16:14.810
No wonder

00:16:14.860 --> 00:16:15.980
he sautéed those vegetables.

00:16:16.740 --> 00:16:18.280
He minced the meat,

00:16:18.560 --> 00:16:20.880
wrapped it up

00:16:20.930 --> 00:16:22.370
with the fatty fish skin to make the rolls

00:16:22.580 --> 00:16:23.710
and fried them.

00:16:24.300 --> 00:16:25.570
He didn’t play safe at all

00:16:25.610 --> 00:16:28.000
even when the stakes are so high!

00:16:28.090 --> 00:16:29.240
Good job! Well done!

00:16:39.170 --> 00:16:40.980
The result is clear, kid.

00:16:43.000 --> 00:16:43.850
It’s too late.

00:16:44.800 --> 00:16:45.810
What’s late, father?

00:16:45.980 --> 00:16:47.140
What do you mean?

00:16:47.390 --> 00:16:51.020
By the time Mao rolled the fish,

00:16:51.560 --> 00:16:53.550
it had become

00:16:53.600 --> 00:16:54.960
less fresh.

00:16:55.110 --> 00:16:56.110
How come?

00:16:56.510 --> 00:16:58.900
As creative as Mao’s dish is,

00:16:59.600 --> 00:17:00.980
Lei En’s dish

00:17:01.030 --> 00:17:03.660
is likely to taste better

00:17:03.720 --> 00:17:04.860
for the perfect timing.

00:17:05.150 --> 00:17:05.740
Are you saying

00:17:05.790 --> 00:17:07.910
Mao’s fish is less good?

00:17:08.030 --> 00:17:10.190
We won’t get any younger

00:17:10.520 --> 00:17:12.900
and neither will fish get any fresher.

00:17:13.790 --> 00:17:14.660
No way would Mao

00:17:14.790 --> 00:17:16.970
not know the time.

00:17:17.160 --> 00:17:18.000
He knew it!

00:17:18.410 --> 00:17:19.710
I mean, he’s a Super Chef!

00:17:19.760 --> 00:17:20.610
He wouldn’t make that mistake!

00:17:21.560 --> 00:17:22.160
That said,

00:17:22.950 --> 00:17:25.020
there’s still hope, Mao.

00:17:26.050 --> 00:17:28.040
Let's taste it.

00:18:13.980 --> 00:18:15.150
What is that?

00:18:29.350 --> 00:18:30.750
What am I eating?

00:18:31.030 --> 00:18:32.360
That fish is still alive!

00:18:39.230 --> 00:18:43.410
So good! The fish is swimming in my mouth!

00:18:43.550 --> 00:18:45.370
It's more than fresh!

00:18:54.030 --> 00:18:56.690
The combination of fish and vegetables

00:18:56.700 --> 00:19:01.660
delivers an authentic flavor!

00:19:02.350 --> 00:19:03.950
This spring roll is as tasty

00:19:04.060 --> 00:19:06.770
as Lei En’s sashimi cooked to the freshest.

00:19:06.950 --> 00:19:10.390
Everything in the roll is flavorful!

00:19:11.670 --> 00:19:13.860
How come the fish still tastes so good

00:19:14.030 --> 00:19:16.380
when it was cooked way past the ideal time?

00:19:18.740 --> 00:19:20.200
I know what I’m doing.

00:19:20.320 --> 00:19:21.990
I'll bring this fish back to life.

00:19:22.470 --> 00:19:23.700
Impossible!

00:19:28.180 --> 00:19:28.940
Did he...?

00:19:36.170 --> 00:19:37.200
Your... your hand is burned!

00:19:38.380 --> 00:19:39.520
Mao’s burned?

00:19:40.040 --> 00:19:41.810
Mao, what happened?

00:19:42.050 --> 00:19:43.730
Don’t tell me you...

00:19:44.750 --> 00:19:45.380
That's right.

00:19:46.190 --> 00:19:49.650
I heated the third knife over the fire

00:19:50.720 --> 00:19:52.990
to preserve the freshness of the meat.

00:19:53.780 --> 00:19:54.390
You...

00:19:55.880 --> 00:19:56.610
Heat?

00:19:57.270 --> 00:19:58.840
That’s it!

00:19:59.660 --> 00:20:01.390
When he used his knife

00:20:01.450 --> 00:20:02.710
to mince the fish,

00:20:03.740 --> 00:20:05.790
the hot surface

00:20:05.840 --> 00:20:07.160
seared the fish skin

00:20:07.590 --> 00:20:08.940
and locked

00:20:08.980 --> 00:20:09.960
the juice inside.

00:20:12.100 --> 00:20:13.700
So the mince

00:20:14.220 --> 00:20:15.800
was already cooked

00:20:16.070 --> 00:20:18.710
and remained fresh.

00:20:20.420 --> 00:20:22.210
The third knife made of

00:20:22.260 --> 00:20:23.480
the steel wire and the Hundred-Hole Knife

00:20:24.040 --> 00:20:25.020
worked surprisingly well

00:20:25.070 --> 00:20:26.540
once heated.

00:20:27.150 --> 00:20:28.330
That’s why he...

00:20:28.710 --> 00:20:30.760
Yes. He held that heated knife

00:20:30.800 --> 00:20:32.470
with bare hands.

00:20:35.780 --> 00:20:37.910
Lei En would give up his right hand

00:20:37.950 --> 00:20:39.170
to slice the fish

00:20:40.800 --> 00:20:44.610
just like Mao would get burned to cook.

00:20:49.810 --> 00:20:51.310
You’re brave, kid.

00:20:51.860 --> 00:20:52.850
Likewise.

00:21:08.890 --> 00:21:10.700
Mao’s spring roll is a winning dish.

00:21:11.170 --> 00:21:12.470
No one has ever done that.

00:21:12.560 --> 00:21:14.820
I disagree. Lei En should win

00:21:14.870 --> 00:21:17.390
because he delivered the best taste

00:21:17.520 --> 00:21:19.030
in the simplest form.

00:21:20.280 --> 00:21:21.060
They’ve been in there

00:21:21.110 --> 00:21:22.070
for far too long.

00:21:22.310 --> 00:21:23.640
They must be divided on the result.

00:21:27.910 --> 00:21:28.740
They’re out.

00:21:39.920 --> 00:21:41.520
We've made the decision.

00:21:42.460 --> 00:21:44.560
The winner

00:21:45.090 --> 00:21:46.600
of this Knife Skills Competition is...

00:23:14.976 --> 00:23:17.020
Preview of the next episode

00:23:18.279 --> 00:23:21.667
The Legendary Cooking Utensils have now awakened
from its centuries-long slumber

00:23:21.761 --> 00:23:23.619
and revealed its mysterious appearance.

00:23:24.278 --> 00:23:26.409
Oh, what's that light?

00:23:27.346 --> 00:23:28.893
Next episode, Chūka Ichiban!

00:23:29.146 --> 00:23:30.391
The Legendary Cooking Utensil!

00:23:30.485 --> 00:23:31.954
The Secret of the Forever-Spirit Knife!

00:23:32.359 --> 00:23:33.676
It will definitely be interesting!
